        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "vgwV8",
          "name": "AR/Body",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "fill": "$bg",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "padding": [
            8,
            0,
            64,
            0
          ],
          "alignItems": "center",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "YazIy",
              "name": "Prose Column",
              "width": 726,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "D23UZQ",
                  "name": "Lead",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Choosing your first foil feels deceptively simple — it is just a thin blade with a handle, after all. But the weapon you learn on shapes how quickly your hand learns to relax, how you feel the point land, and whether practice feels like a fight with your equipment or a conversation with your opponent.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 19,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "XeMXs",
                  "name": "H2 Grip",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Grip: French vs pistol",
                  "fontFamily": "Archivo",
                  "fontSize": 26,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UYsMk",
                  "name": "Body 1",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The French grip is a straight handle that lets you hold the weapon further back for extra reach and offers a wide range of subtle point control. It rewards patience and fine finger work, which is exactly why many coaches start beginners on it — it teaches the hand to steer the blade rather than muscle it around.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 17,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "G5rjI",
                  "name": "Body 2",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The pistol grip, by contrast, locks the hand into a fixed, ergonomic shape. It feels secure and powerful from day one, but that same security can hide bad habits. If you can, try both for a few lessons before you commit — the right answer depends on your hand, not on fashion.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 17,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "TR9Fu",
                  "name": "Pull Quote",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "stroke": "$ink",
                  "strokeWidth": {
                    "left": 3
                  },
                  "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                  "strokeLinejoin": "round",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    4,
                    0,
                    4,
                    24
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Qekzh",
                      "name": "Quote Text",
                      "fill": "$ink",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Your first foil should disappear in your hand — you should think about the touch, not the tool.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.4,
                      "fontFamily": "Archivo",
                      "fontSize": 24,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "fontStyle": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "N1SSFA",
                  "name": "Inline Image",
                  "clip": true,
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 380,
                  "fill": {
                    "type": "image",
                    "enabled": true,
                    "url": "images/generated-1783895107641.png",
                    "mode": "fill"
                  },
                  "cornerRadius": "$radius"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g2TMI",
                  "name": "H2 Weight",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Weight & balance",
                  "fontFamily": "Archivo",
                  "fontSize": 26,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "LjY3P",
                  "name": "Body 3",
                  "fill": "$ink",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A foil that balances close to the guard feels light and quick, favouring fast, flicking attacks and nimble defence. One balanced further down the blade feels planted and stable, which some fencers prefer for controlled, deliberate play. Neither is correct — but as a beginner, err toward the lighter, guard-heavy feel so your arm stays fresh through a full lesson.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 17,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "vTn2o",
                  "name": "Tips List",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 12,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "oOmQW",
                      "name": "Tip",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "lSUzM",
                          "name": "Dash",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "content": "—",
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "E991E",
                          "name": "Text",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Pick the lightest blade you can control cleanly, not the heaviest you can lift.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "jtHzi",
                      "name": "Tip",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "aty63",
                          "name": "Dash",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "content": "—",
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "ttJTJ",
                          "name": "Text",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Check that the guard has no sharp edges and the pommel is tight before every session.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "OmQ6y",
                      "name": "Tip",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "hz5T1",
                          "name": "Dash",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "content": "—",
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "zpHXo",
                          "name": "Text",
                          "fill": "$ink",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "Grip lightly — if your knuckles are white, the foil is driving you.",
                          "lineHeight": 1.7,
                          "fontFamily": "Inter",
                          "fontSize": 17,
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "I4dgA3",
                      "name": "Tip",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "gap": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "B9OrU",
